{#
    Deliberately no <label> before the button -- unlike form_element.zetem
    (text/select/textarea inputs, which need a separate label), a button's
    own visible text is {{$label}} inside the tag itself.

    $attributes already carries this button's own name/type/value
    (ButtonElement::generateHTML()) -- rendered the same
    foreach-over-$attributes way form_element.zetem renders its own
    opening tag, not the attributes() helper (that function only handles
    an Attributes object or ['attributes' => Attributes], not a plain
    array like this one -- it silently returns '' for this shape, which
    is why every button here used to render with no attributes at all).
#}
<button {% foreach($attributes as $key => $value): %}{{ $key }}="{{ $value }}" {% endforeach %}>{{$label}}</button>
